WEBVTT

00:15.730 --> 00:18.330
I’ll never forgive you.

00:19.860 --> 00:21.790
I’ll never…

00:24.330 --> 00:27.250
I’ll ne…

00:31.000 --> 00:33.380
I’ll never forgive you.

00:48.060 --> 00:52.030
Ghost Cat

01:16.470 --> 01:20.810
The blue moon illuminated

01:20.850 --> 01:24.770
your wandering shadow.

01:25.390 --> 01:29.270
I could never tell you all I wanted to say.

01:29.270 --> 01:34.190
It was so very frustrating.

01:34.280 --> 01:38.070
I think about your faked smile,

01:38.660 --> 01:42.700
and forget all the hot tears we shed.

01:43.160 --> 01:45.370
What do these empty husks,

01:45.410 --> 01:51.210
those empty eyes of yours, reflect, my dear?

01:51.960 --> 01:56.420
The transient quarter moon

01:56.800 --> 01:58.590
hides in a rift in the clouds,

01:58.550 --> 02:00.970
as darkness seeps up from the ground.

02:01.010 --> 02:05.430
Tell me the truth, please.

02:05.770 --> 02:07.600
Are you so despondent

02:07.690 --> 02:11.980
that you still sit alone, sighing?

02:12.440 --> 02:15.070
Prelude

02:20.020 --> 02:29.540
It is with great pride that I open
this subway station for business.

02:29.540 --> 02:31.370
Thank you. Thank you.

02:31.370 --> 02:32.660
Yes, thank you!

02:32.660 --> 02:33.910
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

02:33.910 --> 02:34.790
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

02:34.790 --> 02:35.920
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

02:34.790 --> 02:35.920
Sir, we should get going.

02:35.920 --> 02:36.920
Sir, we should get going.

02:39.340 --> 02:42.470
Thank you. Thank you.

02:46.550 --> 02:49.270
Thank you! Thank you!

02:49.600 --> 02:52.230
Everyone on the platform, please stand back!

02:52.680 --> 02:55.780
We’ll need to see your tickets before boarding!

02:56.190 --> 02:58.360
Don’t push! No pushing, please.

03:00.900 --> 03:04.280
Um, is this where car number four will be boarding?

03:07.280 --> 03:09.740
Um, no, it’s not.

03:09.740 --> 03:11.620
This is the first car.

03:11.620 --> 03:13.660
Only VIPs can get in there.

03:13.660 --> 03:14.420
Over there.

03:14.420 --> 03:15.660
Aw, all that way?

03:15.660 --> 03:16.830
What’s with him?

03:16.830 --> 03:20.380
Oh my, that huge pack must be heavy!

03:21.590 --> 03:24.050
He looks kind of handsome, though.

03:24.050 --> 03:26.260
He must be one of those sandwich board advertisers.

03:26.260 --> 03:29.310
Yeah, looks like it. Thank you so much, sir!

03:29.840 --> 03:31.310
Excuse me! Sorry!

03:31.850 --> 03:33.350
Excuse me!

03:33.350 --> 03:35.220
Sorry!

03:35.890 --> 03:37.020
Sorry!

03:39.270 --> 03:42.780
Stand back! Stand back!

03:54.040 --> 03:56.540
Excuse me, everyone. Let me through.

03:56.540 --> 03:57.380
Hey, wait!

03:59.830 --> 04:02.290
Thank you for providing security, Detective.

04:11.020 --> 04:12.520
Aw man. It’s not fair!

04:13.510 --> 04:16.230
I want to ride up there, with the mayor!

04:16.230 --> 04:17.310
Excuse me.

04:18.480 --> 04:20.690
Will the train be back by this afternoon?

04:21.440 --> 04:26.440
It loops back after four stops, so it should be less than an hour.

04:32.370 --> 04:34.920
Well, this is a banner day!

04:35.490 --> 04:36.750
Four more minutes!

04:37.620 --> 04:42.710
I’d like to embark on the second stage as soon as possible.

04:42.710 --> 04:45.880
Of course! I trust you implicitly, sir.

04:45.880 --> 04:47.720
You have our full support.

04:48.340 --> 04:50.510
I’m Moria, from the Morning News.

04:50.510 --> 04:52.730
Allow me to congratulate you on the new station.

04:53.300 --> 04:55.390
How do you feel right now?

04:56.140 --> 05:00.180
I’m extremely pleased to meet the expectations of my citizens.

05:00.180 --> 05:02.270
I suppose that’s most of what I’m feeling.

05:02.270 --> 05:04.770
Well said, sir! Well said, indeed!

05:03.940 --> 05:04.780
What suck-ups.

05:04.780 --> 05:05.570
What suck-ups.

05:06.950 --> 05:10.320
Hey, ink-slinger, let’s leave it at that, shall we?

05:23.170 --> 05:24.960
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

05:24.960 --> 05:26.460
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

05:26.460 --> 05:27.670
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

05:27.670 --> 05:28.500
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

05:28.500 --> 05:30.140
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

05:50.570 --> 05:54.110
This train’s atmosphere is so pleasant, isn’t it?

05:54.110 --> 05:55.620
Yes, it is indeed.

05:56.280 --> 05:59.120
The riff-raff on my last ride were so unpleasant.

05:59.120 --> 06:01.040
Yes, well they are all rather rank.

06:01.040 --> 06:03.540
I could barely breathe!

06:15.590 --> 06:16.890
And the very first train, to boot!

06:22.020 --> 06:24.980
I could hardly believe I won the drawing.

06:24.980 --> 06:29.060
I’ve so been looking forward to this.

06:29.060 --> 06:31.820
Yes, so have I!

07:46.390 --> 07:47.900
Was there an accident?

07:47.900 --> 07:49.860
All right. Everyone remain calm.

07:50.690 --> 07:51.570
Oh wow!

07:52.440 --> 07:53.950
Geez.

07:57.870 --> 07:59.240
What?

07:59.240 --> 08:01.200
What? What? Wha—

08:20.050 --> 08:21.770
Was it my imagination?

08:21.770 --> 08:23.680
Mr. Mayor?

08:23.680 --> 08:24.810
Where’s everyone else?

08:25.220 --> 08:27.020
Where’d they go?

08:25.220 --> 08:27.020
How did…

08:27.020 --> 08:29.150
They’re all gone.

08:29.150 --> 08:31.900
Oh, thank you so much for earlier!

08:31.900 --> 08:33.770
Oh, not at all.

08:34.190 --> 08:38.490
We apologize for the inconvenience.

08:38.490 --> 08:47.080
We have discovered a foreign object blocking the tracks,

08:44.070 --> 08:44.830
Where is this?

08:45.700 --> 08:47.330
The first car.

08:47.080 --> 08:51.090
and are taking the necessary precautions.

08:47.330 --> 08:49.160
The first car?

08:49.160 --> 08:50.210
Hey, you!

08:51.500 --> 08:53.290
What are you doing here?

08:53.290 --> 08:56.800
Hey, it’s nothing to shout about.

08:57.210 --> 08:59.670
Don’t be rude to the passengers.

08:59.670 --> 09:00.510
But—

09:01.050 --> 09:05.510
Surely none of them have any
insight into these strange occurrences.

09:06.560 --> 09:08.020
I’ll

09:08.020 --> 09:10.150
return to my seat, then.

09:15.190 --> 09:17.820
I’ll be going, too!

09:28.790 --> 09:30.460
It’s too heavy!

09:31.290 --> 09:32.410
I can’t budge it.

09:32.410 --> 09:35.130
Uh. Let me try it!

09:35.130 --> 09:37.130
Useless women.

09:38.170 --> 09:39.930
This is Kinoshita, the driver.

09:40.300 --> 09:42.260
Station One, come in.

09:46.760 --> 09:48.520
That’s strange.

09:48.520 --> 09:50.150
Allow me.

09:50.930 --> 09:52.020
Thank you!

09:52.020 --> 09:55.900
Old man just can’t contain himself, can he?

09:58.570 --> 10:00.530
What’s the matter?

10:00.530 --> 10:02.650
Why aren’t we moving?

10:02.650 --> 10:03.620
Hey, you!

10:04.410 --> 10:05.320
What’s going on?

10:05.320 --> 10:06.950
Thank you so much!

10:06.950 --> 10:13.000
I’ll have to have it modified so that anyone can open it.

10:18.340 --> 10:20.750
Where are the other cars?

10:45.110 --> 10:46.780
Mr. Mayor?

10:47.540 --> 10:50.120
Who’s driving this thing?

11:24.110 --> 11:27.740
I’ll never forgive you.

11:41.300 --> 11:44.140
Did you just say you wouldn’t forgive me?

11:46.560 --> 11:49.430
Did you just say you wouldn’t forgive me?

11:52.690 --> 11:55.610
Did anyone say that?

11:59.110 --> 12:00.070
No.

12:02.030 --> 12:03.700
It was just my imagination.

12:03.700 --> 12:05.120
Oh no, how scary!

12:05.490 --> 12:07.080
My imagination…

12:05.790 --> 12:07.080
What’s the matter with this train?

12:07.080 --> 12:08.950
What’s the matter with this train?

12:09.330 --> 12:11.410
Aren’t you in control?

12:11.410 --> 12:14.370
I’ve used every tool at my disposal!

12:14.370 --> 12:16.590
We can’t even contact the surface.

12:17.670 --> 12:20.550
I’ll never get promoted now.

12:20.550 --> 12:25.590
I thought that today would go so well.

12:23.090 --> 12:25.590
We’re in the tunnel the whole way, so it really is pretty scary.

12:25.590 --> 12:26.470
We’re in the tunnel the whole way, so it really is pretty scary.

12:26.470 --> 12:28.890
We’re in the tunnel the whole way, so it really is pretty scary.

12:26.510 --> 12:28.890
10:05 a.m., sudden stop.

12:28.890 --> 12:30.930
Passengers vanish. Cause unknown.

12:32.140 --> 12:38.690
Hey Newsman, don’t you get sick if you write on the train?

12:39.780 --> 12:44.280
I’ve been doing my job for twenty years. I’m quite used to it.

12:48.740 --> 12:50.240
What’s wrong, boy?

12:50.240 --> 12:52.830
Goodness! Don’t scare me like that!

12:51.910 --> 12:52.830
Um…

12:53.460 --> 12:56.250
There was just a…

13:12.810 --> 13:13.930
Here it is.

13:13.930 --> 13:15.230
Who are you?

13:15.230 --> 13:17.060
It’s the Sandwich Board Man.

13:17.060 --> 13:18.230
Newsman!

13:33.910 --> 13:36.460
How?

13:36.460 --> 13:38.040
There’re no other cars back there.

13:38.500 --> 13:41.590
How’d you get in here?

13:41.590 --> 13:44.260
As you saw,

13:44.260 --> 13:47.050
I came from the next car along.

13:49.050 --> 13:52.810
I am a medicine seller.

13:52.810 --> 13:54.060
Huh?

13:54.350 --> 14:00.480
I have to dress like this these days, for my wares to sell.

14:00.480 --> 14:03.030
Still, it’s awfully pretty.

14:03.530 --> 14:05.320
You saw that, didn’t you?

14:05.320 --> 14:09.870
I don’t know why, but we can’t get out of the door from here.

14:11.700 --> 14:15.200
Just a minute ago, the mayor…

14:15.620 --> 14:16.870
Fell out.

14:17.960 --> 14:21.630
Don’t finish his sentences! That’s creepy!

14:22.460 --> 14:25.260
The train’s moving of its own accord.

14:25.260 --> 14:29.010
It’s as though a fox spirit has a hold of it.

14:30.680 --> 14:34.510
This is not a fox spirit’s doing.

14:34.510 --> 14:35.100
I know that.

14:35.970 --> 14:36.980
It’s just a figure of speech.

14:37.850 --> 14:39.690
The mayor

14:40.850 --> 14:42.770
was killed by a Mononoke.

14:49.240 --> 14:49.990
A Mononoke?

14:49.990 --> 14:51.820
Stop that! Don’t be creepy!

14:51.820 --> 14:53.410
Get your craziness out of here!

14:53.410 --> 14:54.330
It was an accident, that’s all!

14:54.330 --> 14:56.410
But the train’s moving on its own.

14:55.240 --> 14:56.410
Of course it was an accident!

14:56.410 --> 14:57.120
Of course it was an accident!

14:57.120 --> 14:58.660
He’s yelling again.

14:58.660 --> 15:00.330
You didn’t see anything!

15:01.040 --> 15:03.090
I can tell

15:03.840 --> 15:05.920
even without having seen.

15:06.300 --> 15:07.090
It moved by itself!

15:24.400 --> 15:25.320
What are those?

15:26.150 --> 15:28.110
They’re scales.

15:28.110 --> 15:29.650
They’re scales.

15:30.610 --> 15:32.860
Their alignment

15:33.240 --> 15:36.540
tells me the Mononoke’s position.

15:36.540 --> 15:39.540
tells me the Mononoke’s position.

15:39.540 --> 15:41.000
tells me the Mononoke’s position.

15:59.560 --> 16:02.440
You are all connected.

16:02.440 --> 16:06.900
The Mononoke has placed all those involved in this car.

16:06.900 --> 16:09.730
Connected? We’re all meeting for the first time.

16:09.730 --> 16:10.740
That’s right!

16:10.740 --> 16:13.660
I just won my ticket in a raffle!

16:11.530 --> 16:13.660
How would you say we’re connected?

16:13.660 --> 16:17.200
You should all know that.

16:18.950 --> 16:21.000
I think I do know one of you!

16:21.000 --> 16:21.960
What?

16:21.960 --> 16:24.920
Me too. I remember one person.

16:24.920 --> 16:27.500
I remember one of you, as well.

16:27.500 --> 16:28.500
Me too.

16:28.500 --> 16:29.550
Who, then?

16:33.300 --> 16:34.090
You too?

16:34.090 --> 16:36.050
I don’t know anyone.

16:36.050 --> 16:39.260
Yeah, I’ve no idea what this is about, either.

16:39.260 --> 16:40.640
My.

16:40.640 --> 16:44.350
To think that four of the six here recognize the same person.

16:44.350 --> 16:47.610
Would you all be able to tell me more?

16:47.610 --> 16:50.570
I don’t remember any of them.

16:50.570 --> 16:51.860
Oh, right!

16:51.860 --> 16:55.950
Let’s have all your names, ages and
professions, along with where you say you met me.

16:55.950 --> 16:58.240
Yes, right. That’s a good idea.

16:58.240 --> 17:00.330
I’m Nomoto Chiyo, aged twenty-one.

17:00.330 --> 17:03.120
I’m a waitress at a café across from the station!

17:03.120 --> 17:05.960
A shining example of a career woman.

17:07.290 --> 17:08.460
Well, yeah.

17:08.460 --> 17:10.130
Don’t be ridiculous!

17:10.130 --> 17:11.510
I never went to that café!

17:11.510 --> 17:12.800
Yes you did!

17:12.800 --> 17:15.840
You came in on an investigation, didn’t you, Detective?

17:15.840 --> 17:17.680
When was this?

17:17.680 --> 17:19.010
Three or four months ago, right?

17:19.010 --> 17:20.060
Yeah, exactly!

17:20.060 --> 17:21.390
Hey, how did…

17:23.600 --> 17:24.980
Oh, Detective!

17:24.980 --> 17:30.440
You were outside smoking while your
partner questioned me, so I didn’t recognize you.

17:30.440 --> 17:33.280
Ah. I’m Yamaguchi Haru, a widow.

17:33.280 --> 17:34.150
Age?

17:34.150 --> 17:34.820
Don’t be rude.

17:34.820 --> 17:37.200
Thirty-five.

17:35.700 --> 17:37.200
You didn’t have to tell him.

17:37.200 --> 17:40.280
And what happened to your husband?

17:40.280 --> 17:43.750
He died five years ago of an illness of the lungs.

17:43.750 --> 17:45.460
I currently live with my mother-in-law.

17:45.460 --> 17:46.960
Just the facts, ma’am!

17:46.960 --> 17:48.460
You really don’t remember?

17:48.460 --> 17:50.500
Unlike you, I’m a busy man!

17:50.500 --> 17:53.130
I can’t remember everyone I meet. Now, say when you met me!

17:53.130 --> 17:56.470
Let’s see, what cures amnesia?

17:53.130 --> 17:56.470
You have to give your name and age first, Detective.

17:57.010 --> 17:58.800
You’re a willful young woman.

17:59.140 --> 18:01.810
Kadowaki Shakei, forty years old.

18:01.810 --> 18:03.010
I’m a police officer.

18:03.350 --> 18:05.100
Then I’ll give you a hint.

18:05.100 --> 18:07.810
It was about a regular customer at our shop.

18:07.940 --> 18:10.860
One of those… Modern Girls, they call them.

18:10.860 --> 18:14.780
That’s not all. She was totally gorgeous, too!

18:14.780 --> 18:17.860
I was so jealous!

18:18.490 --> 18:21.240
Unfortunately, though, she got hit by a train and died.

18:21.240 --> 18:22.700
I didn’t mean to!

18:28.540 --> 18:31.040
I didn’t mean to.

18:31.040 --> 18:32.880
Morning News. Train accident.

18:32.880 --> 18:34.090
Morning News. Train accident.

18:34.090 --> 18:35.630
Oh, that!

18:35.630 --> 18:39.050
That’s right. I remember. You
were driving at the time, weren’t you?

18:39.050 --> 18:40.300
Your name was…

18:40.300 --> 18:43.600
Kinoshita Bunpei, twenty-eight.

18:43.600 --> 18:45.430
It was just an accident!

18:45.430 --> 18:49.600
She jumped off the bridge, killing herself, and
my train just happened to be passing through.

18:50.060 --> 18:51.560
Jumped off…

18:50.060 --> 18:51.560
I told you then, I didn’t mean to do it!

18:51.560 --> 18:53.150
I told you then, I didn’t mean to do it!

18:53.150 --> 18:56.110
We get it! Calm down. It wasn’t your fault.

18:56.110 --> 18:59.700
We determined it was a clear suicide.

18:56.110 --> 18:57.780
I see.

18:57.780 --> 18:59.700
So, that’s it.

18:59.700 --> 19:02.070
You look a bit pale.

19:02.070 --> 19:04.830
Shall I make you a tonic?

19:04.830 --> 19:07.000
No, I’m fine.

19:07.000 --> 19:08.200
And who are you?

19:08.200 --> 19:10.080
Moria Kioshi.

19:10.080 --> 19:15.130
Normally I have a desk job at a newspaper, but they
were shorthanded today and sent me out in the field.

19:15.670 --> 19:18.590
He was the victim’s boss.

19:18.590 --> 19:21.970
She was a writer, then? How nice.

19:21.970 --> 19:23.720
She was pretty famous, if I remember.

19:23.720 --> 19:24.600
What was her name?

19:24.600 --> 19:26.680
I remember her now!

19:26.680 --> 19:28.140
Ichikawa Setsuko!

19:28.140 --> 19:31.440
I was so jealous that she had her name in the paper!

19:31.440 --> 19:33.360
This is some mistake!

19:35.020 --> 19:36.900
I don’t know any of you!

19:36.900 --> 19:40.030
Why do I have to stay locked in here?

19:40.030 --> 19:42.160
Let me off, please!

19:42.820 --> 19:44.530
What does he mean?

19:44.530 --> 19:45.870
I wonder.

19:45.870 --> 19:48.080
Hey, what’s your name?

19:48.080 --> 19:49.620
Kobayashi Masao.

19:49.620 --> 19:50.790
Where do you go to school?

19:50.790 --> 19:54.670
I just graduated from elementary
school, and I work delivering milk.

19:54.670 --> 19:56.750
It must be hard, so early in the morning.

19:57.210 --> 19:58.630
Morning?

19:58.630 --> 20:03.680
If I remember correctly, it was about 5
a.m. when my train passed under the bridge.

20:03.680 --> 20:05.800
Kirigahara Bridge, eh?

20:07.060 --> 20:09.310
A delivery boy, you say.

20:09.310 --> 20:11.020
That’s right.

20:11.890 --> 20:14.690
The dots are finally connected.

20:41.510 --> 20:42.720
Oh.

20:44.430 --> 20:45.720
My word.

20:46.050 --> 20:48.140
There was a woman holding a cat, there.

20:48.140 --> 20:51.060
There was a woman holding a cat, there.

21:04.150 --> 21:05.490
It’s a Ghost Cat.

21:06.990 --> 21:09.950
To be continued

21:11.750 --> 21:19.250
Without you, I just can’t smile.

21:20.380 --> 21:30.310
I walk this banal town,

21:30.310 --> 21:36.390
feeling such intense emotions.

21:36.940 --> 21:42.780
I know that if I could treasure them and live on,

21:42.860 --> 21:52.080
I would need nothing else.

21:52.740 --> 22:00.250
The summer flowers that bloomed in the sky

22:00.250 --> 22:06.550
Come falling down, dancing in the wind.

22:06.630 --> 22:09.890
I can barely recall the night sky

22:09.890 --> 22:13.180
where they all came tumbling down,

22:13.180 --> 22:24.030
so what I can still recall is all the more precious.
